        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: خطط",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "خطط — khaṭṭaṭa — \"to make plans\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "يخطط أخي لرحلة في الصيف. yukhaṭṭiṭu akhī li-riḥla fī aṣ-ṣayf. My brother is planning a trip in the summer."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يخطط, yukhaṭṭiṭ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes لـ for what is planned."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "خطط (khaṭṭaṭa) is built on the native Arabic root kh-ṭ-ṭ, \"to draw a line\" (Lane). Khuṭṭa, a plan, which you know, is from the same root: a plan is lines drawn ahead."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
